{"id":50940,"ord":103,"n_segments":161,"prev":50939,"next":50941,"doc":{"id":"66600","title":"66600_Teddy Wilson oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Teddy Wilson","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/66600/","url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=66600"},"chapter":"Regional bands, politics and travel abroad","title":"Each city's collection of bands","category":"venue_city_scene","summary":"They list New York, Chicago, St. Louis and Kansas City bands, and the big hotel bands that came to Chicago.","period":"1920s-30s","year_from":1920,"year_to":1959,"words":134,"start":[144,0],"end":[144,8],"url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=66600#s50940","tags":{"places":[{"name":"Chicago","focus":0,"type":"city"},{"name":"St. Louis","focus":0,"type":"city"},{"name":"Kansas City","focus":0,"type":"city"}],"venues":[{"name":"Smalls Paradise","focus":0,"city":"New York"},{"name":"Cotton Club","focus":0,"city":"New York"},{"name":"Savoy Ballroom","focus":0,"city":"New York"},{"name":"Renaissance Ballroom","focus":0,"city":"New York"}],"bands":[{"name":"Duke Ellington Orchestra","focus":0,"leader":"Duke Ellington"},{"name":"Cab Calloway Orchestra","focus":0,"leader":"Cab Calloway"},{"name":"Baron Lee and the Blue Rhythm Band","focus":0,"leader":"Baron Lee"},{"name":"Teddy Hill Orchestra","focus":0,"leader":"Teddy Hill"},{"name":"Willie Bryant Orchestra","focus":0,"leader":"Willie Bryant"},{"name":"Benny Carter's band","focus":0,"leader":"Benny Carter"},{"name":"Chick Webb Orchestra","focus":0,"leader":"Chick Webb"},{"name":"Jeter-Pillars Orchestra","focus":0,"leader":null},{"name":"Ben Pollack Orchestra","focus":0,"leader":"Ben Pollack"},{"name":"Ben Bernie Orchestra","focus":0,"leader":"Ben Bernie"},{"name":"Kansas City Nighthawks","focus":0,"leader":null},{"name":"Coon-Sanders Orchestra","focus":0,"leader":null}]},"people":[{"name":"Benny Carter","qid":"Q356715","n":1},{"name":"Willie Bryant","qid":"Q730199","n":1},{"name":"Ben Pollack","qid":"Q816581","n":1},{"name":"Ben Bernie","qid":"Q816444","n":1},{"name":"Coon-Sanders","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Teddy Hill","qid":"Q1530476","n":1},{"name":"Baron Wilkins","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Baron Lee","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Ralph (Chick Webb band)","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Tim (Chicago bandleader)","qid":null,"n":1}],"story":{"theme":33,"theme_name":"Chicago: the jazz migration and its clubs","community":59,"community_name":"Going north: working the Chicago jazz scene","core":false},"blocks":[{"p":144,"b":0,"s":"MR. HINTON","x":"Yeah."},{"p":144,"b":1,"s":"MR. WILSON","x":"Some of those bands that played the Small's Paradise, and the Cotton Club Band, Duke and Cab and Baron Lee and Baron Wilkins, was that it? The Blue Ribbon Band. And all those bands, the Savoy, Teddy Hill, Willie Bryant, Benny Carter. And Ralph was with Chick. And the bands that used to play the Renaissance, the West Indian jazz bands."},{"p":144,"b":2,"s":"MR. HINTON","x":"Right. Well, maybe we're going in circles because Jeter-Pillars (PHONETIC) was coming up from St. Louis to Chicago."},{"p":144,"b":3,"s":"MR. WILSON","x":"Yeah, St. Louis and Kansas City."},{"p":144,"b":4,"s":"MR. HINTON","x":"Kansas City, was coming to Chicago. And the big white bands, Ben Pollack was coming in Chicago, and Ben Bernie and Tim."},{"p":144,"b":5,"s":"MR. WILSON","x":"And the Kansas City Nighthawks went to Chicago, and Coon-Sanders."},{"p":144,"b":6,"s":"MR. HINTON","x":"Coon-Sanders, right."},{"p":144,"b":7,"s":"MR. WILSON","x":"So each town had its collection of bands."},{"p":144,"b":8,"s":"MR. HINTON","x":"And we had those great hotels."}]}